  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Use the following information to answer questions 1 - 4. </para>
<blockquote>
  The graph of \(f(x) = 2x + 6\) is graphed below. Answer the questions about the linear function and its key features.
</blockquote>
<para><figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE WITH AN \(x\)-intercepts OF −3 AND \(y\)-intercepts OF 6."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/883d5444bd5bb58e4fd98f9e360dd63cace83db2"/></media></figure></para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the value of \(f(-3)\)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>0</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What key feature of the linear function is the point \((-3,0)\)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The \(x\)-intercept, or zero</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the slope of the linear function?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>2</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What part of the linear function is the point \((0, 6)\)?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The \(y\)-intercepts
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<para>Use the following information to answer questions 5 - 8. </para>
<blockquote>
  The amount of money Adam saves in dollars is shown in the graph below.
</blockquote>
<figure><media alt="GRAPH THAT SHOWS THE TOTAL AMOUNT OF MONEY IN DOLLARS AS A FUNCTION OF NUMBER OF DAYS. THE FUNCTION IS A LINE WITH A POSITIVE SLOPE THAT PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 3) AND (1, 6)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a963f822c76db76cac7225e978193e50fed19143"/></media></figure><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the \(y\)-intercept of the graph?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The point is \((0,3)\).
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What does the \(y\)-intercepts mean in the context of the problem</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary.</para>
    <para>When Adam started saving, he already had 3 dollars on
      day 0.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the slope?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The slope is 3.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What does the slope mean in the context of the problem</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary.</para>
    <para>Every 1 day, Adam saves 3 dollars.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<para>Use the following information to answer questions 9 - 12.</para>
<blockquote>The graph of \(f(x) = 13x + 2\) is graphed below. Identify the appropriate label for each key feature of the graph.</blockquote>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4de93ead19af6557e95474c5ea621808fdf1b873"/></media></figure></para>

<!--Q3a-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the key feature labeled \(A\) on the graph?
      </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:
    </para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(A\), (0, 2), is the \(y\)-intercept.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q3b-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the key feature labeled \(B\) on the graph?
      </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:
    </para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(B\), (-6, 0), is the \(x\)-intercept or zero.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q3c-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the key feature labeled \(C\) on the graph?
      </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:
    </para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(C\), (0, 0), is the origin.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q3d-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the key feature labeled \(D\) on the graph?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:
    </para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(D\), \(\frac13\), is the slope.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
